# The erasure's two tile layers. The map is `Map0014.json`, and what it is
# for is there: two events that `EraseEvent` themselves and a jump to this
# same map, `tests/test_erase_event.py`. The field is bare so that a cell
# where nothing is drawn looks like any other.

# 20x15, 300 tiles per layer
# The two tile layers, in reading order: one id per tile, 20 per line.
# These are the ids the binary stores; what turns them into pictures is
# the chipset. Edited by hand, the count has to stay the same.
